<title>SWITZERLAND: SIG sees improved 1997 results.</title>
<headline>SIG sees improved 1997 results.</headline>
<dateline>NEUHAUSEN, Switzerland 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss mechanical engineering group SIG Schweizerische Indistriegesellschaft (SIG) expects results to improve across all its operations in 1997, chief executive David Syz told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect an improvement in every way,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>SIG has room to make gains operationally as well as by bolstering its presence abroad, he said, adding he could imagine entering more partnerships with foreign companies.</p>
<p>SIG also has potential to boost internal synergy, Syz said.</p>
<p>SIG lifted 1996 group net to 88.6 million Swiss francs from 70.1 million.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
